       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"PDF Automation Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is PDF automation?\", \"a\": \"PDF automation is the use of automated processes to handle routine document tasks such as generating, organizing, or routing files without constant manual input. The four examples above split between reading PDFs that arrive and producing PDFs that go out.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I set up PDF automation?\", \"a\": \"Start with one document type and a handful of real copies of it, then write down where those PDFs arrive and which values your team needs from them. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a> creates the app, its records, and its review screen from a plain-English prompt. When a customer switches to a new form layout later, you change the app by prompting.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does PDF automation fill in a fillable form from my records?\", \"a\": \"Upload the fillable PDF and map each of its boxes to a column in your records or a question on a web form. The app then writes each value into its matching box and saves a new filled copy for every record. If you cannot click into the boxes of your form, ask for the text to be placed by position on the page instead.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can PDF automation create documents from a template I already use?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Give the app a PDF you sent recently as the model, and it lays out each new document the same way, filled from the record behind it. For quotes that also need follow-up after they go out, <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/proposal'>proposal automation</a> covers what happens once the client opens the document.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should I look for in PDF automation software?\", \"a\": \"Look at how it handles your own documents first, including your worst scan, before you compare feature lists. Then check where the extracted values are stored, whether you can take them with you, and whether the price rises with every document processed. In an app Emergent builds, the records stay in your own database, and runs have no task cap.\"}, {\"q\": \"What happens when PDF automation misreads a field?\", \"a\": \"In an app Emergent builds, a field read with low confidence goes to a person before it reaches your records. Decide which fields always need a person anyway, such as bank details, and keep a log of each correction so you can see which senders cause the most of them.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can PDF automation turn survey results into a report?\", \"a\": \"Yes. When a survey closes, the app can total the responses and lay them out as a PDF with one chart per question, then email it to the people who need it. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/ranking'>ranking survey</a>, for example, becomes a report that lists each option by its average rank.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can PDF automation merge several documents into one packet?\", \"a\": \"Set a fixed order for the documents and a trigger, such as a job being marked complete, and the app merges whatever PDFs are attached in that order. Decide ahead of time what happens when one is missing: hold the packet and alert the job owner, or send it with a note on the first page about the gap.\"}, {\"q\": \"Are free PDF automation tools enough for a small team?\", \"a\": \"Try a free option on a real batch first. If your team still retypes values from the PDFs into another system afterward, you need something that connects to that system, not only a tool that edits files. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I use PDF automation to send each person their own copy?\", \"a\": \"Keep one record per person and one layout, and the app fills a separate PDF for each record and emails it to the address on that row. After a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/leadership'>leadership survey</a>, for example, each manager can get a PDF with only their own team's scores. Send the first batch to yourself and open a few side by side before it goes out.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
